ghidra for Debian
-----------------

The program lives in /usr/lib/ghidra, read-only. Commands:

  ghidra                    graphical interface (ghidraRun)
  ghidra-analyzeHeadless    automated analysis (support/analyzeHeadless)
  ghidra-pyghidraRun        PyGhidra (support/pyghidraRun)

Java: Ghidra needs a JDK 21 or later, not a JRE: scripts are compiled at run
time. The launcher takes the JDK found on the PATH (update-alternatives
--config java); if it finds no suitable one, it asks once for a JDK home and
remembers it. Set JAVA_HOME_OVERRIDE in
/usr/lib/ghidra/support/launch.properties to force one for every user.

Release name: a build from the source tree is labelled "DEV" by upstream
(Ghidra/application.properties), official NSA archives "PUBLIC". User
settings therefore go to ~/.config/ghidra/ghidra_<version>_DEV, apart from
those of an official archive install.

PyGhidra: on Debian the system Python is externally managed (PEP 668), so
ghidra-pyghidraRun offers to create a virtual environment in the user
settings directory; python3-venv is needed for that.

Extensions are installed per user (user settings directory), the read-only
installation is never modified.

arm64: 7-Zip-JBinding has no native library for this architecture. The
built-in zip support is enabled in launch.properties, and the 7zip package
(7z/7zz commands) lets Ghidra open other archive formats.

